  "c-gap": {
   "idea": "A black rock and a white house hold open a gap of lit fog, and the wet stair climbs out of the dark into the town's light.",
   "shape": "Three big flat shapes: the rock a black wedge of a few straight runs with one thin wet rim of sky, C a true-white block whose gable is the frame's one crisp silhouette, and a soft shelf of lit fog across the gully behind the Landing; the wet treads a ladder of sky-lit lines up into it; beyond the Landing everything soft, in pearl.",
   "colour_script": "Key: ultramarine only in the near darks, blue-grey sky, pearl beyond the Landing; shade takes the fog's colour. Accent: one warm family in three strengths: the lantern globes near white, C's lit wall and the fog shelf peach, the windows amber. The one white: the Landing's globe and C's lantern-lit corner. Darkest: the rock wedge and the lantern posts.",
